            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0506" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/940.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Mexican
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: The following telegram
                    has been received from a representative of the United States district attorney
                    at Douglas, Ariz.:</p>
                <p>[Same telegram as that quoted in above telegram to the chargé d’affaires.]</p>
                <p>Our embassy at the City of Mexico has not reported as to whether any unauthorized
                    action of subordinate officials gives substance to this painful report, of which
                    I fpel your excellency would wish to be apprised.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
